  "goodToKnow": "Die Legierung is an alloy: Bronze (copper and tin), Messing (brass: copper and zinc), Stahl (iron and carbon), Edelstahl (stainless steel). Legieren means to alloy, and in cooking to thicken a sauce or soup with egg yolk or cream. From Latin ligare (to bind). Euro coins use the Nordic Gold alloy for the 10, 20 and 50 cent pieces. Plural: die Legierungen."
